  "worked_solution": "First, we find the mixed partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(a{x}^{2}y-4{y}^{2}+3) \\\\  & =a{x}^{2}-8y \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(2{x}^{3}+bxy-8) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+by\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have the identity\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a{x}^{2}-8y=6{x}^{2}+by.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of ${x}^{2}$ and $y,$ respectively, we see that $a=6$ and $b=-8.$",
